// The keeper of the rune seal (examples/keeper.luau talks from this file). Yarn Spinner's
// language: `Name: line`, `-> option`, `<<command>>`, $facts. The seal's script sets
// $runes_lit and $seal_opened, so the keeper knows how far you are; the quest it gives
// (quests/sealed_bridge.quest) follows the same facts. See "Story" in the scripts README.

title: Start
when: $seal_opened
position: 0,540
---
<<bow>>
Keeper: The door stands open. Listen... the crystal sings again.
<<once>>
    Keeper: A hundred winters I kept that seal. I had forgotten what the light looked like.
    <<set $keeper_thanked to true>>
    -> What now?
        Keeper: Now the way across is ours. Watch.
        <<cutscene cutscenes/courtyard>>
        Keeper: Go well, traveller. The courtyard will remember you.
    -> I should go.
        Keeper: Then go with the light at your back.
<<else>>
    => Keeper: Every lantern burns a little brighter tonight.
    => Keeper: The herald has not flown so high since I was young.
    => Keeper: You again. The runes still hum your name. <<if visited_count("Start") > 3>>
<<endonce>>
===

title: Start
when: once
position: 0,0
---
<<bow>>
Keeper: Ah. A traveller, and at this hour.
Keeper: I keep the seal. Three runes, one door, and a hundred winters since anyone opened it.
-> Who sealed it?
    <<jump Lore>>
-> Can it be opened?
    <<jump Offer>>
-> I'll leave you to it.
    Keeper: Most do. The door does not mind.
===

title: Start
when: always
position: 0,280
---
=> Keeper: Back again?
=> Keeper: {$runes_lit} of three. The seal is listening. <<if $runes_lit > 0>>
=> Keeper: The drone has been watching you. Mind its light. <<if quest_active("sealed_bridge")>>
-> Tell me about the seal again.
    <<jump Lore>>
-> I'll try the runes. <<if quest_state("sealed_bridge") == "inactive">>
    <<jump Offer>>
-> Nothing. Goodbye.
===

title: Lore
position: 440,0
---
Keeper: Those who built this courtyard were afraid of what sleeps behind that door.
Keeper: Or of who would come looking for it. The old songs disagree.
Keeper: Each rune answers a touch: the left stone, the right, and the plate in the floor.
-> And if all three are lit?
    Keeper: Then the seal lets go. That is all a seal is: a promise kept until it is not.
    <<if quest_state("sealed_bridge") == "inactive">>
        <<jump Offer>>
    <<endif>>
-> Enough stories.
===

title: Offer
position: 440,300
---
<<if quest_active("sealed_bridge")>>
    Keeper: You carry the task already. {$runes_lit} of three, so far.
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Keeper: Then the seal is yours to try.
<<raise_staff>>
<<quest start sealed_bridge>>
Keeper: Touch each rune. When the door sinks, come and tell me what you saw.
===
